  "notes": "Waiver filing, cash basis, Exhibit A by fund (p1/p3 General, Street, Enterprise, Library, Cemetery, Fire; p2/p4 Keno, Rev. Sharing, Amplifund; p1/p3 Total column includes p2/p4). Enterprise Fund is business-type (named Water in the p6 transfer schedule; its spending printed on line 29 General Government and line 35 Capital Improvements); all other funds governmental. Governmental lines = Total column minus the Enterprise column. Transfers per attachment p6 (total 167,617.52): General -> Amplifund 33,900, Water 16,159.02, Streets 23,900; Fire -> General 3,000; Water -> General 2,000; Streets -> General 13,500, Amplifund 40,000; Amplifund -> Streets 35,158.50. Enterprise (Water) net transfers +14,159.02 are business-type transfers_net. Library and Rev. Sharing had no disbursements (printed '-'), so no expenditure detail_totals for them. Capital Improvements has no printed function (generic Capital outlay label, as FY2023). Beginning/ending cash are line 3/line 24 subtotals (net cash + investments) minus Enterprise, as in FY2023. County Treasurer balances (996.39 / 751.65) printed below the statement are not included. Roll-forward governmental: 287,244.55 + 237,293.99 - 210,170.22 + 151,458.50 - 165,617.52 = 300,209.30 (equals FY2023 beginning); business: 15,550.70 + 53,829.58 - 51,166.76 + 14,159.02 = 32,372.54. No supplementary schedules; detail is per fund column of Exhibit A. Read pages 1-6 of 6"
